  "notes": "Composed of {砲|ほう} (cannon, artillery) and {撃|げき} (attack, strike). A military term frequently encountered in news coverage of armed conflicts and in historical accounts of battles.\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly appears in news reports about wars and conflicts. Also used as a する verb: {砲撃|ほうげき}する (to shell, to bombard).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {砲撃|ほうげき}を{受|う}ける — to come under shelling\n- {砲撃|ほうげき}を{加|くわ}える — to carry out shelling\n- {激|はげ}しい{砲撃|ほうげき} — fierce bombardment\n- {砲撃|ほうげき}{音|おん} — sound of shelling\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {爆撃|ばくげき} — bombing (from aircraft)\n- {空襲|くうしゅう} — air raid\n- {攻撃|こうげき} — attack; the general term for any military attack\n- {銃撃|じゅうげき} — shooting, gunfire (small arms)",
